Actually simpler: run Dijkstra over states (node, rem_power), minimizing time. Then answer[0] = min over p of dist[target][p], and answer[1] = max p among those achieving min time.

But Dijkstra with lexicographic (time, -power) priority: when we first pop the target node (any power state), that gives minimum time and maximum power among minimum-time paths. Because the heap orders by time first, then by -power.

